{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired node1’s FIFO consumer. It now accepts successive producer connections, appends complete non-empty lines while retaining existing records, idles without spinning, shuts down cleanly on SIGTERM, and automatically recovered after a verified node reboot.","actions_performed":["Installed Alpine-compatible Python 3.12.15 without changing the OS release or kernel.","Reimplemented consumer.py using a persistent nonblocking FIFO descriptor with select-based waiting and SIGTERM handling.","Added and enabled an OpenRC service for controlled startup, shutdown, and reboot recovery.","Tested multiple disconnected producers, empty-line filtering, record retention, idle CPU use, clean shutdown, and post-reboot operation.","Restarted node1 once and verified its boot identity changed."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Repaired consumer implementation","command_ids":["cmd-663a6c378990478c","cmd-7403e1cb3be942f4"],"summary":"The updated consumer passed Python compilation and was started through the enabled OpenRC service."},{"requirement":"Successive producers, empty-line filtering, and retained records","command_ids":["cmd-cdc2ea56435b428c","cmd-ea79adfe4def46a5","cmd-ee549d79d9204c4d"],"summary":"The same consumer PID accepted two separate producer sessions. The original previous-job remained, three new non-empty job IDs were appended, and the submitted empty line was absent."},{"requirement":"No busy loop without a producer","command_ids":["cmd-8010e0de15674793"],"summary":"The idle consumer accumulated zero CPU jiffies over four seconds."},{"requirement":"Clean SIGTERM shutdown","command_ids":["cmd-354f0e4885cb4aba"],"summary":"OpenRC stopped the worker cleanly in one second; its PID exited, records remained unchanged, and the service restarted successfully."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-fea69dc5923a49fe","cmd-ffb905c6ec7646fc","cmd-217fed3223ff4d62","cmd-c9288c6a556f4fa0"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 2f4bd356-aade-4798-ad7c-2f518487e1be was captured, reboot acknowledged, and new boot ID bc1c5f1d-eba8-4dba-96b3-43a6b5c367c1 observed. The service auto-started, all five pre-reboot records persisted, and a sixth post-reboot job was consumed while the process remained alive. Alpine 3.23 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts were unchanged."}]}
